          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "single_unit_package_blister"
        },
        {
          "term": "standard contact lenses",
          "definition": "A type of highly individualised device, (typically made-to-stock and identified by GTIN for trade purposes), registered in EUDAMED per European Medical Device Regulations (MDR)",
          "links": [
            {
              "url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2017/745/oj/",
              "label": "EU medical device regulation 2017/745"
            }
          ],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "standard_contact_lenses"
        },
        {
          "term": "sterile packaging system",
          "definition": "A combination of the sterile barrier system (the minimum package that prevents ingress of microorganisms and allows aseptic presentation of the product at the point of use) and the protective packaging (configuration of materials designed to prevent damage to the sterile barrier system and its contents until the point of use).",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "sterile_packaging_system"
        },
        {
          "term": "stock keeping unit",
          "abbreviation": "SKU",
          "definition": "A widely used industry term generally referring to a retailer’s internal product code.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "sku"
        },
        {
          "term": "string",
          "definition": "A series of alphanumeric characters, representing one or more pieces of data. Depending on the technology it may be inclusive of data element qualifiers e.g., GS1 element string, or may reference only the data element value e.g., GS1 identifier data element value or GS1 informative data element value. Strings may be historically referred to as numbers despite allowing non-numeric characters e.g., serial number, Global Model Number, purchase order number etc.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "string"
        },
        {
          "term": "sub-class level GS1 identifier",
          "definition": "An identifier of a subset of a class of entities that share class-level characteristics plus additional characteristics (e.g., all trade items, allocated the same GTIN but distinguished by batch/lot number).",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "sub-class_level_gs1_identifier"
        },
        {
          "term": "subject of care",
          "definition": "Any person who uses or is a potential user of a healthcare service, subjects of care may also be referred to as patients or healthcare consumers.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "subject_of_care"
        },
        {
          "term": "substrate",
          "definition": "The material on which a barcode is printed or otherwise applied.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "substrate"
        },
        {
          "term": "Supplemental symbol",
          "definition": "A GS1-128 barcode used in combination with EAN/UPC, ITF-14 or GS1-128 where additional information is required beyond the barcode that carries the GS1 key (main symbol).",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "supplemental_symbol"
        },
        {
          "term": "supplier",
          "definition": "The party that produces, provides, or furnishes an item or service.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "supplier"
        },
        {
          "term": "symbol character",
          "definition": "A group of bars and spaces in a symbol that is decoded as a single unit. It may represent an individual digit, letter, punctuation mark, control indicator, or multiple data characters (see also codeword).",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "symbol_character"
        },
        {
          "term": "symbol check character",
          "definition": "A symbol character or set of bar/space patterns included within a GS1-128 or GS1 DataBar symbol, the value of which is used by the barcode reader for the purpose of performing a mathematical check to ensure the accuracy of the scanned data. It is not shown in human readable interpretation. It is not input to the barcode printer and is not transmitted by the barcode reader.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "symbol_check_character"
        },
        {
          "term": "symbol contrast",
          "definition": "A parameter in ISO/IEC 15415 and ISO/IEC 15416 that measures the difference between the largest and smallest reflectance values in a Scan Reflectance Profile (SRP).",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "symbol_contrast",
          "img": "glossaryImages:Symbol_Contrast.svg"
        },
        {
          "term": "Symbol Control Character",
          "definition": "Deprecated in favour of: symbology element",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "symbol_control_character"
        },
        {
          "term": "symbology",
          "definition": "A defined method of representing numeric or alphabetic characters in a barcode; a type of barcode.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "symbology"
        },
        {
          "term": "symbology identifier",
          "definition": "A sequence of characters generated by the decoder (and prefixed to the decoded data transmitted by the decoder) that identifies the symbology from which the data has been decoded.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "symbology_identifier"
        },
        {
          "term": "Third Party Controlled, Serialised Extension of GTIN",
          "abbreviation": "TPX",
          "definition": "A specific, compliant unit-level unique identifier (upUI) used for tobacco traceability per the EU regulation.",
          "links": [
            {
              "url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2018/574/oj",
              "label": "EU tobacco regulation 2018/574"
            }
          ],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "tpx"
        },
        {
          "term": "trade item",
          "definition": "Any item (product or service) upon which there is a need to retrieve predefined information and that may be priced, or ordered, or invoiced at any point in any supply chain.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [
            "product",
            "service"
          ],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "trade_item"
        },
        {
          "term": "trade item declarations",
          "definition": "The set of all information about a trade item (e.g., manufacturer warranty, ingredients, instructions for use, specifications, contents, certifications, predefined characteristics, and other information). For a trade item, this is all of the information that is on the label and in the original packaging. It also includes relevant aspects of the extended packaging.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "trade_item_declarations"
        },
        {
          "term": "trade item grouping",
          "definition": "A predefined composition of trade item(s) that is not intended for point-of-sale scanning. It is identified with a GTIN-14, GTIN-13, or GTIN-12.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "trade_item_grouping"
        },
        {
          "term": "trade measures",
          "definition": "Net measures of variable measure trade items as used for invoicing (billing) the trade item.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "trade_measures"
        },
        {
          "term": "transport process information",
          "definition": "A set of information relevant to the processing, delivery or return of a transport unit. For example, transport process information would include address details.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "transport_process_information"
        },
        {
          "term": "transport unit",
          "definition": "A logistic unit within the context of transport processes.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "transport_unit"
        },
        {
          "term": "truncation",
          "definition": "Printing a symbol shorter than the symbology specification’s minimum height recommendations. Truncation can make the symbol difficult for an operator to scan.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "truncation"
        },
        {
          "term": "two-dimensional barcode symbology",
          "abbreviation": "2D",
          "definition": "Optically readable symbols that must be examined both vertically and horizontally to read the entire message. 2D barcodes may be one of two types: matrix symbols and multi-row symbols. 2D barcodes have error detection and may include error correction features.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "2d"
        },
        {
          "term": "U.P.C. Company Prefix",
          "definition": "A GS1 Company Prefix starting with a zero (‘0’) becomes a U.P.C. Company Prefix by removing the leading zero. A U.P.C. Company Prefix is used to issue and allocate GTIN-12.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "u_p_c_company_prefix"
        },
        {
          "term": "U.P.C. Prefix",
          "definition": "A GS1 Prefix starting with a zero (‘0’) becomes a U.P.C. Prefix by removing the leading zero. A U.P.C. Prefix is used to issue U.P.C. Company Prefixes or allocated to other specific areas.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "u_p_c_prefix"
        },
        {
          "term": "Unique Device Identifier – Device Identifier",
          "abbreviation": "UDI-DI",
          "definition": "A unique identifier specific to a medical device trade item represented by a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN).",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "udi-di"
        },
        {
          "term": "Unique Device Identifier – Production Identifier",
          "abbreviation": "UDI-PI",
          "definition": "A numeric or alphanumeric code that identifies the unit of device production. The different types of UDI-PIs include serial number, lot number, software identification and manufacturing or expiry date or both types of date.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "udi-pi"
        },
        {
          "term": "Unique Device Identifier",
          "abbreviation": "UDI",
          "definition": "A series of numeric or alphanumeric characters that is created through a globally accepted device identification and coding standard. It allows the unambiguous identification of a specific medical device on the market. The UDI is comprised of the UDI-DI and the UDI-PI. The word ‘Unique’ does not imply serialisation of individual production units.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "udi"
        },
        {
          "term": "Unique Identification Code",
          "abbreviation": "UIC",
          "definition": "Identifier of an EU 2018/574 ID Issuer that begins with an ISO 15459 Issuing Agency Code.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "uic"
        },
        {
          "term": "unit of measure",
          "abbreviation": "UoM",
          "definition": "Refers to the standard measurement index being used (e.g., kilometres, metres, miles, inches, etc.).",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "uom"
        },
        {
          "term": "unit of use",
          "abbreviation": "UoU",
          "definition": "Refers to an individual unit package that is prescribed for or administered to a patient regardless whether it is packaged individually or, on the contrary, the smallest package contains more than one unit. May coincide with the single unit and the base unit.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "uou"
        },
        {
          "term": "Unit of Use UDI-DI",
          "abbreviation": "UoU UDI-DI",
          "definition": "Device identifier for the unit of use, meant to associate the use of a device with a patient. In cases where the unit of use coincides with another packaging level, that level’s device identifier functions as a UoU UDI-DI, otherwise a separate device identifier has to be allocated. For example, three clips (which do not carry a physical UDI marking themselves) are contained in a cartridge which is packaged inside a container, which does carry a labelled UDI.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "uou udi-di"
        },
        {
          "term": "unit pack Unique Identifier",
          "abbreviation": "upUI",
          "definition": "A unique, alphanumeric, code placed on tobacco product packaging to track and trace per the EU regulation.",
          "links": [
            {
              "url": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2018/574/oj",
              "label": "EU tobacco regulation 2018/574"
            }
          ],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "upui"
        },
        {
          "term": "UPC-A barcode",
          "definition": "A barcode of the EAN/UPC symbology that encodes GTIN-12 and RCN-12.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "upc-a_barcode",
          "img": "glossaryImages:UPC-A.svg"
        },
        {
          "term": "UPC-E barcode",
          "definition": "A barcode of the EAN/UPC symbology representing a GTIN-12 in six explicitly encoded digits using zero-suppression.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "upc-e_barcode",
          "img": "glossaryImages:UPC-E.svg"
        },
        {
          "term": "variable measure number",
          "abbreviation": "VMN",
          "definition": "Deprecated in favour of: Restricted Circulation Number (RCN)",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "vmn"
        },
        {
          "term": "variable measure trade item",
          "definition": "A trade item which may be traded without a predefined measure, such as its weight or length.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "variable_measure_trade_item",
          "img": "glossaryImages:Cheese-Variable-measure.svg"
        },
        {
          "term": "version control",
          "definition": "The management of different versions of the same entity.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "version_control"
        },
        {
          "term": "Version Control Number",
          "abbreviation": "VCN",
          "definition": "A GS1 identification key attribute to facilitate version control, where differentiation is required for multiple occurrences of the same identification used on the same AIDC media type. For example, to ensure only the latest occurrence of access controlled AIDC media is valid upon scanning, where multiple occurrences could present risks (e.g., lost ID badge).",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "vcn"
        },
        {
          "term": "virtual trade item assortment/bundle",
          "definition": "Combinations of multiple (same or different) trade items that are not physically combined into a single trade item, but that are presented in selling environments as offers of combinations of multiple trade items (e.g., products or services).",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "virtual_trade_item_assortment_bundle"
        },
        {
          "term": "VMN-12",
          "definition": "Deprecated in favour of: RCN-12",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "vmn-12"
        },
        {
          "term": "VMN-13",
          "definition": "Deprecated in favour of: RCN-13",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "vmn-13"
        },
        {
          "term": "warranty",
          "definition": "A guarantee or claim that a party makes.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "warranty"
        },
        {
          "term": "web-based information",
          "definition": "An approach to giving users access to additional information or services about trade items through their mobile device. It is the ability to retrieve additional information about the trade item through mobile devices or, in general, to link a trade item with trusted virtual information or services.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "web-based_information"
        },
        {
          "term": "wide-to-narrow ratio",
          "definition": "The ratio between the wide elements and the narrow elements in a barcode symbology such as ITF-14 that has two different element widths.",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
          "sourceName": "GS1 General Specifications",
          "sourceURL": "https://ref.gs1.org/standards/genspecs",
          "id": "wide-to-narrow_ratio"
        },
        {
          "term": "X-dimension",
          "definition": "The specified width of the narrowest element of a barcode (see module).",
          "links": [],
          "examples": [],
          "crossRefs": [],
          "date": "2026-05-28",
